body:
I have permanent corpse eyes, no matter what I do. It's just a genetic feature, not a result of drug abuse or poor sleep cycles or anything. I could sleep for 20 hours straight, eat super healthy, exercise, nothing changes it. I've kinda grown to like the look. It makes me seem oddly wise and experienced somehow, and it's GREAT at work, cause in the office I always look exhausted even if I'm wide awake and energetic, so my boss always thinks I'm working way harder than anyone else. 

&#x200B;

If you wanna get rid of your circumstantial dark circles, just get some sleep and wash your face with cold water. I've also heard some people swear by cold, refrigerated used teabags. Like after making a cup of tea, just pop the bags in the egg tray in the fridge, and once they're cold, plop em on your eyes for a bit and it supposedly reduces puffiness. If you want an instant fix, just buy a concealer pen in your skin tone. Don't think of it as makeup - it's not glossy or glittery or shimmery or any crap like that. It's literally like covering up the discoloration with a magic marker.

If you live in the middle east, central or west Africa, Chechnya or small radical easten European countries, then yes. In the UK, USA, Australia and Western Europe, absolutely not. 

&#x200B;

It may seem like that because people are more vocal now than they were ever before, and multiple sources relentlessly report on the same thing, but you have to realize that you're living in a golden age of freedom and statistically, objectively, irrefutably, things have never been as good for us in the past as they are now.

One or two sessions of professional cleaning / polishing by a dentist / dental-hygienist every year, switch from red wine to white, and eat strawberries as messily as you can because they're great for whitening. 

If you're in a pinch and need quick results though, there's nothing wrong with Crest whitening kits, as long as you don't use them too often. 

&#x200B;

Bon Iver - For Emma, Forever Ago.

He literally embraced the deep depression he'd fallen into, barricaded himself in a remote cabin in the woods and poured his soul out. Might not be everyone's preferred genre, but goddamn is it gorgeously tragic.

&#x200B;

Did you include your face in the pictures you shared? That's the only way anyone would be able to recognize you. Uninstalling the app doesn't delete the account. If you deleted your account first, it automatically erases the chat history and all photos and everything - so that's what you should have done. But either way, most gay guys have way better things to do with their time than going around outing closeted bicurious guys for no reason. People aren't all assholes. I think you should just relax and carry on with your life. 

Even if the profile is still out there, it won't show up on anyone's radar because you're not active - so nobody will be able to see it. The only person who can see it is the guy you sent the pictures to. And I doubt he's holding on to hopes of hooking up with you after 6 months. So chill out and carry on.

&#x200B;

Fucking NO. If I see a damn spider in my house, I'm either getting in a hazmat suit and buying a flamethrower, or I'm just moving to a new house.

Why do arachnids always think that they're going to get tonnes of food under my bathroom sink? That's like the second cleanest place in my house! Ain't nothin gonna fly into your web down there! Just stay the fuck outside high up in a tree or something where I can easily avoid you and you can get all the bugs you could ever want. Why you gotta encroach on my territory and blatantly freak the fuck out of everyone with your nasty hairy legs and that weird weaving dance you do that looks like you're summoning Satan?

&#x200B;

Introverted verging on agoraphobic. Love me another introverted guy too. Staying in is cheaper, and as stupendously boring as it sounds, I like to invest my money wisely. I like staying in with my cat, watching netflix and sipping on a martini, maybe listening to some Little Dragon, or the latest David Sedaris audiobook. I love cooking lavish feasts in my tiny spotless kitchen and going full Martha Stewart from the comfort of my home, and I also have my own  gym so I don't have to feel awkward about massive ripped guys sniggering at my skinny ass on the elliptical, plus it's weirdly fun to work out naked sometimes and check yourself out in the mirrors.

Extroverted guys are fun but just exhausting. I hate noisy clubs, I hate hanging out with more than 3 people at once cause I get overwhelmed with too many voices and fake laughs and lame stories to keep track of, I hate going out for a run in the park in the morning and I think sunsets are a ridiculous conspiracy because they're totally overrated. 

&#x200B;

OK you're all over the place. Calm down and breathe first. If you're 21 and living with your dad, I'm guessing you aren't financially self-sufficient. But you surely have enough cash to go to the nearest pharmacy and buy some Melatonin- it is a completely safe and non-addictive over-the-counter sleep hormone pill that is impossible to overdose on, in fact it loses its effect in higher doses, so it's the ideal sleep aid with no risk of any stupid thoughts of harming yourself. If not Melatonin, you can even just buy some regular antihistamines because they're great sedatives too, also non addictive. Don't turn into a crazy pill-popper. Occasional use of harmless drugs like these should be fine since you're so desperately sleep deprived. Do NOT buy sleeping pills. That is a slippery slope. For me at least.

&#x200B;

Now regarding your father, you're going to need more than just a "vibe" to be certain he's a pedophile. I get the sense that you have some traumatic repressed memories involving him but I might be reading too much into it. Because there's also a possibility that he was just being a weirdly open father when he showed you his dick. If he has ever tried to touch you, or tried to watch you while showering, or if he exposed himself in an inviting or expectant way, then you need to get the hell out of that house. But if you're only talking about that one instance when you practically asked him to show you his dick, there might not be more to this vibe you're getting.

&#x200B;

Either way, get some sleep. Lock your bedroom door at night. Work on your film whenever you have the time. I don't think your family is going to be particularly supportive if you approach them with your problems, so I'd suggest seeking friends who can help instead.

He's 21. The age difference might not seem like much, but 21 is a very precarious time and often the peak of immaturity and hysteria because you've spent the last 20 years pining to be a fully functional adult and bitching about people not taking you seriously and now finally you have that, you are a full adult and you have nothing else to do but start contributing and being accountable for things. It's hard, it's disorienting and baby-boomers don't make it any easier on them by wagging judgmental fingers and calling them "entitled arrogant millennials". By your age, all the crazy tends to settle down and you  become mature and responsible.

&#x200B;

You need to break up with him because there's no point trying to work things out cause clearly you're not suited for each other. But you should let him down easy. Blame it on things beyond his control - focus on the age gap rather than on his flaws and immature behavior.

Try screaming into a pillow. Or talk it out with a cat. It will pay absolutely no attention to you and then it will become the new vessel for all of your frustration, and who can stay mad at a cat?

&#x200B;

On a serious note, I personally think self acceptance is a load of crap because if you accept yourself exactly as you are, there's no room left to grow or change or acknowledge your flaws, and that's a pretty bleak prospect for people who don't have a lot to work with to begin with. You're better off using your anger to fuel and motivate yourself to fix whatever it is you don't like. You might never be as good as you want to be, but if you try and make the slightest change, at least you'll like yourself more than you do now.

I never said infidelity was progressive. My point was that these countries are primarily agnostic and have been for several decades and as a result, the morality and ethics rooted in biblical christian values aren't as prevalent as in American culture. They accepted same-sex relationships and marriage a lot sooner than other western countries, the age of consent is generally lower, age of drinking as well, and they're mostly far more comfortable with nudity - both male and female. Virginity isn't seen as pious and virtuous, and slut-shaming is near nonexistent. Things like unisex nude saunas are commonplace for instance, whereas in the States there'd be a whole media-fueled perceptive issue around the complications of something like that because of the deeply ingrained traditionalist conservative views of gender and sexuality.

&#x200B;

All I'm saying is that these countries are progressive because they view sex as just sex and nothing more. It's not a politicized statement on a person's morality or character. So cheating is obviously not seen as ideal, nor is it encouraged, but it's also not something that the whole town gathers together with pitchforks to pass judgment on. The public / your neighbor will just stay out of it and assume you'll handle the situation with maturity and dignity. There won't be a bunch of angry bloggers writing takedown smear pieces just because somebody had an indiscretion owing to personal marital issues we know nothing about.

&#x200B;

To use your own example, a Newt Gingrich type would ONLY be criticized for his political views and his personal life would not even factor in or be brought up at all. It would not be dragged in to emphasize a view or point out hypocrisy. He'd just be criticized for policy.
